estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The gate declares the minimum producer version whose events it can classify by contract tags and partitions issues whose last-seen release precedes it into a named reported class rather than counting them as blocking unclassified faults; A blocked cut names per blocking issue whether it blocked as a genuine unexpected fault or as an event carrying no contract tags; A negative control proves both directions: a fixture issue with usage-class tags is ignored, and the same issue without tags from a pre-contract release appears in the legacy partition and not in the blocking set; Regression evidence records the 2026-08-08 counterfactual that PM-CLI-2Q resolves to invalid_workspace_snapshot_target exit 2 class usage and would have been ignored had its event carried the tags"
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Versioned Sentry producer epoch with reported legacy partition
expected_result: Pre-contract releases are visible but nonblocking; current unknown/no-tag faults remain blocking with explicit reasons
actual_result: "Gate declares minimum producer 2026.8.7, partitions legacy issues, emits missing_contract_tags or unexpected_fault reasons, and passes 60 linked tests"
